            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0829" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-01T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1925—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 1—12:34
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>278. Department’s 282, August 31, 8 p.m. was read to Foreign Office whereupon
                    Embassy was informally advised that British Chargé d’Affaires at Peking would be
                    instructed to cooperate with his American colleague: First, in arranging
                    McEuen’s immediate suspension; second, in endeavoring to obtain as satisfactory
                    assurances as possible that McEuen will be retired in the event of his
                    vindication; and third, in expediting the holding of the judicial inquiry.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Houghton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
